Level 28 is plenty, and yeah i'd only Finger rodney if i was out of
other instakill options. I haven't ascended a wizard before, i wonder
how well the eye offsets the penalty from the amulet of yendor - if
your energy regenerates fast enough then maybe it's only a hit to
hunger. Other, more experienced players can comment on this i'm sure.

And as for the weapon, i prefer the magbane over the staff mainly
because of the cursing scare. If you're wielding a 2h weapon and it
gets cursed, then you're in a world of hurt. It disables both your
hands: you cannot cast spells (remove curse) or open bags (to get your
remove curse scrolls or holy water). So if you do decide to use the
staff, make sure you have one of those items in your main inventory
(and hope that they themselves don't get cursed).

Overall, sounds like you're more than prepared equipment wise. How
about the rest of the ascension kit:

- few c?gold detection (or do the confusion bit), or other means of
detecting traps on the plains
- c?gain level (to escape the sanctum, convenience)
- c?teleport + tele control to get to the sanctum (convenience)
- a way to uncurse items
- a few !Full healing
- as many /Teleport and /Death you can find, some /Slow Monster for air
elementals, /Digging for earth, /Secret Door Detection for the sanctum,
etc

but it sounds like you're good to go! good luck!



